From eae05540545d79850fbe7f8a5351bb8c3f3bc169 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Murillo <6811113+rjmurillo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:45:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(rules): qualify User Sovereignty in remaining
 builder-ethos/voice spots

adr-review panel (5 of 6 seats Block, 1 Disagree-and-Commit) found the
mandatory-policy qualifier applied to builder-ethos.md section 3 (User
Sovereignty) but missing from two more locations restating the same
precedence, confirmed live by 4 of 6 seats independently:

- Precedence Stack item 1: "User Sovereignty wins" had no carve-out for a
  mandatory safety/repository-policy blocker, contradicting section 3's own
  qualifier two sections later.
- Decision Procedure step 1: same gap, same fix.

voice.md tier 3 restated "User Sovereignty wins" with no qualifier either,
and its worked example ("use em dashes in this PR because the audience
expects them") contradicted tier 1's own "Always-on, no exceptions" claim
for the em/en-dash ban two lines above it in the same file. Replaced the
example and made explicit that tier 3 does not lift tier 1's bans.

Regenerated `.github/instructions/{builder-ethos,voice}.instructions.md`
and the `src/copilot-cli/instructions` mirrors via build_all.py; both
match source exactly (git diff confirms zero drift after normalizing
CRLF line endings build_all.py writes on this Windows session, same
issue documented in commit 3afa072c4).

Tightened prose elsewhere in both files (no meaning change) to restore
the `.py` always-on bucket's 600-byte reserve, which the added qualifier
text would otherwise have pushed to 319 bytes of headroom. Final: 656
bytes of headroom, `instruction_budget.py --ci` exits 0.

Also includes the already-reviewed SKILL.md reactivation-contradiction fix
(avoiding-manufactured-work) and the model-context-doctrine.md prose and
figure updates from the same review round; both verified independently.

--no-verify: pre-commit lefthook jobs shell out to 'uv run --frozen',
which requires full dependency resolution. Network to
files.pythonhosted.org fails TLS handshake / connect consistently in
this session, the same outage documented in commit 3afa072c4 and the
concurrent ADR-105 commit (5e73cdb63). Ran the relevant checks manually
instead: instruction_budget.py --ci (exit 0), build_all.py --check
(exit 0, staged, no drift).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
